<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=kerosene">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Chemistry</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kerosene</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Kerosine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kerosene, also called paraffin, is a combustible hydrocarbon liquid distilled from petroleum and used as a fuel for lamps, stoves and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jet-engine">jet engines</a>; the distilling of crude oil into kerosene was first written about in the 9th century by the Persian scholar Rāzi. The modern industry began with lamp oil from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>: Abraham Gesner coined the name for a fuel he claimed to have demonstrated in 1846, and James Young patented his paraffin oil in 1850. After Edwin Drake's well of 1859, American refiners switched to petroleum, and kerosene largely replaced whale oil.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kerosene.jpg" alt="Kerosene" width="320" height="548" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: R. Henrik Nilsson · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:4_litre_Kristallfotogen_kerosene_can_by_Aktiebolaget_Lyse_Sweden_early_20th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>9th century</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Persia</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Rāzi · <a href="/empire/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>The modern industry began with lamp oil from coal: Abraham Gesner claimed priority from 1846 and James Young patented his process in 1850.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/distillation">Distillation<span>c. 1200 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/oil-well">Oil well<span>347 CE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=kerosene">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
